From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Playport <dev@playport.invalid>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 19:44:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] WOW64: run the WoW64 module on the iOS host

Build the WoW64 module with FEX_IOS_HOST and give it what that
configuration of FEXCore needs:

- the JIT pool's write offset, from WINE_IOS_JIT_RW/RX as the ARM64EC
  module reads it, before InitCore; the process refuses to start
  without it;
- the ARM64EC module's placement: FEX's host structures in the host
  band, and code buffers in the JIT pool (allocated as EC_CODE, which
  is what Wine's iOS allocator moves into the pool); FEX's VirtualAlloc2
  keeps a caller's own address requirements instead of adding the WoW64
  default beside them;
- the guest window. iOS has no low 4 GB, so Wine keeps a WoW64 guest's
  address space at a host base B (guest g is host B + g). The module
  reads B from its paired TEB32 (host address minus its guest self
  pointer) and checks it against PEB32. The decoder reads guest code
  from B + EIP, and every block translates its memory operands below
  KUSER_SHARED_DATA inline (the sub-floor hooks of fex-port 0060); the
  rest faults low and Wine's Mach handler services it in the window;
- guest-versus-host addresses at the module's edges: the FS base, the
  syscall/unix-call bridge and EIP/ESP stay guest; the syscall return
  address, its argument block and the unix-call parameters are read
  through the window; tracker notifications and queries are in host
  addresses, and the InvalidationTracker invalidates FEX's code by guest
  address;
- the ARM64EC-only hooks FEXCore calls: no JIT-pool aliases, no Mono
  bridge (Wine publishes it to the x86-64 module only), FFS counters;
- _time64 in FEX's CRT, which an iOS diagnostic in Core.cpp calls;
- no thread_local in the module (it has no TLS directory, and Wine runs
  the CPU before the loader sets up a thread's TLS block): the IR
  capture mark is a plain global there, and AllocWatch names a thread
  by its TEB.

Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-03-portal2-fex-wow64.md
Offered-upstream: no; depends on the iOS port's JIT pool and Wine's window
